title: singing_storm_start
tags: gas_giant
---
Your sensors pick up a rhythmic signal coming from inside the gas giant's crushing atmosphere. It's not random static; it's a distress beacon using an outdated Ark encryption code. The source is deep—approaching hull-crush depth. #line:singing_storm_start_00
-> Dive and Retrieve <<if has_item("resource_fuel", 2)>> #line:singing_storm_start_01
    <<take_item resource_fuel 2>>
    <<if roll(100) <= 60>>
    <<jump singing_storm_success_dive>>
    <<else>>
    <<jump singing_storm_fail_dive>>
    <<endif>>
-> Deploy Drone #line:singing_storm_start_02
    <<jump singing_storm_drone_success>>
-> Ignore #line:singing_storm_start_03 #leave
    <<stop>>
===

title: singing_storm_success_dive
tags: 
---
The pressure screams against your hull, but you snag the object. It's a 'Black Box' from Ark Mission 12. The audio log is terrifying\: 'The clouds... they aren't clouds. They are billions of microscopic machines eating the ship.' #line:singing_storm_success_dive_00
-> Continue #line:singing_storm_success_dive_01
    <<give_item item_ancient_data_log 1>>
    <<damage_ship 5>>
    <<reveal_clue clue_ark_mission_12>>
    <<stop>>
===

